{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>A solemn rest, a sabbath of holiness</b> — He placed שבתון before שבת and afterwards קודש. And in the section ויקהל He placed קודש before שבת: 'it shall be for you קודש שבת שבתון לה׳' — to teach that one adds from the profane to the holy at its entry and at its exit, that rest is required before the essence of holiness arrives and after the holiness has departed. And likewise in one place it is written את שבתותי תשמרו — He placed שבת before שמירה, and in another place He placed שמירה before שבת, like that which we learned in the Mishnah: the tailor must not go out with his needle near dark — and שמירה after it, for it is forbidden to benefit from labor done on the Sabbath, such as bathing in a bathhouse that was heated for the needs of an Israelite."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:14.909308205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}